+### 5c. Close the loop (optional for Pulse/Next/CRMA builds)
+
+Every demo can end with an action, not just an insight. `close_loop.py` reads the story (from the generated data) and **builds ONE follow-up into the demo org**: Flows the audience fires during the meeting. Claude Code is not running at demo time. A follow-up = a **record action** + **one trigger**.
+
+| Story signal | Action | What the follow-up creates |
+|---|---|---|
+| Named at-risk entities (default) | `task` | One `AiO Alert:` Task per top-N at-risk entity (due today+2) |
+| Operational failure (stockout, SLA, defect, route, quality…) | `case` | One escalation Case with the drill path and at-risk list |
+| Segment-wide behavior change (enrollment, participation, adoption…) | `campaign` | One recovery Campaign targeting the culprit segment |
+
+| Trigger | How it's fired in the demo | Default for |
+|---|---|---|
+| `slack_button` | Insight card in Slack → **Create follow-ups** link → confirmation screen | `task` / `campaign` |
+| `record_triggered` | A Task with Subject `AiO Signal: {Metric} …` (a threshold breach) runs it automatically | `case` |
+
+When the follow-up runs, a Notify Flow posts an "action taken" card to Slack through Salesforce's native Slack action. If the org has no Slack connection, it posts to Chatter instead.
